PLAN=plan(8,'Sets and classification','Part IV · Shape, structure and measure',14,'Fairness and development','Representation, Systems','Sets organise membership and overlap; clear definitions and representations prevent double counting and make survey claims testable.','When two groups overlap, what can we know about the missing intersection, and how does that change a decision?','In order for a student to organise information, students must define categories, represent overlap, check totals and explain how a definition changes a conclusion.',S,explore,application,assessment,mixed,ready,check,[S[0]['diagram'],S[1]['diagram'],S[2]['diagram']],['Use set notation, elements and subsets.','Represent union, intersection and complement with Venn diagrams.','Classify number families and place values on the real line.','Interpret survey counts and justify decisions with stated denominators.'],'set · element · subset · empty set · universal set · union · intersection · complement · Venn diagram · natural · whole · integer · rational · irrational · real',key='Form',sourcepages='155–173; answers 232–234')
